t":[{"type":"text","text":"Puerto Rico and «Las rosas blancas»","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"She had moved to Puerto Rico earlier that decade, where the producer and television actor Elín Ortiz — recently separated from the vedette Iris Chacón — became her manager; they married in 1974 and stayed married until his death in 2016. Her weekly variety show ran on WAPA-TV, Canal 4, every Sunday night until 1985, mixing elegant staging with guest slots for artists from across Latin America; a special episode Ortiz wrote and directed for the same channel, «Las rosas blancas», won a Peabody Award in the United States."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Film, a producer from Madrid, and a cancelled telenovela","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In the early 1980s she starred opposite the Mexican actor Julio Alemán in the film «Prohibido amar en Nueva York», whose soundtrack produced two more hits, «Tiempo» and «Para llegar». In 1985 she recorded «Verdades desnudas», produced by the Spanish singer-songwriter Camilo Sesto, and the following year she joined Iris Chacón, the Dominican-Mexican actor Andrés García and the Puerto Rican singer Yolandita Monge in the telenovela «Escándalo», which underperformed and was cut short."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Family, Miami, and «Escándalo TV»","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Her son Shalim, born in 1979, went on to his own career as a singer and actor; the family moved to Miami in 1988, and Charytín had twins, Alexander and Sharinna, around 1990. She returned to television full-time in 2002 to host the celebrity gossip show «Escándalo TV» for Univision’s TeleFutura, alongside Marisa del Portillo, Felipe Viel and Lilia Luciano, and later fronted her own program, simply titled «Charytín», on Mega TV from 2013."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Legacy","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In 2003 the Asociación de Cronistas de Espectáculos de Nueva York gave her its Premio Extraordinario ACE por Distinción y Mérito, and in 2007 the Asociación de Cronistas de Arte awarded her El Soberano for her career in Dominican entertainment. In 2022, at seventy-three, she published an autobiography, «El tiempo pasa... ¡pero yo no!», writing for the first time about the private difficulties behind more than fifty years spent, by her own description, as a whirlwind of a public persona."}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', id, 1 FROM artists WHERE slug = 'charytin'
